{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1045 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "6a38758b78a76709f14597f96b44cab6b999db1755bb398ae80867da16a87989" :edb/db-before-t 1044 :edb/db-after-t 1045 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534357 50 #inst "2026-10-11T19:35:22.988Z" 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186228087 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420163 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186228087 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420163 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186229163 1038 #edb/ref 17592186420166 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186229643 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186229643 1071 "Given that the differential equation\n$y^{′} - 2y = 6e^{2x}$,\nhas the complementary solution $y_{c}(x) = Ae^{2x}$, find the particular solution to the equation.$y_{p}(x) =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534357 17592186045417 false] [17592186229643 1071 "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-2y=6{e}^{2x},\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x}$, find the particular solution to the equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186229643 1074 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nWe see that the right-hand side is $6{e}^{2x},$ and ${e}^{2x}$ is a term in the complementary solution, so we assume that a particular solution takes the form \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha x{e}^{2x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nWe calculate the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ using the product rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & =(\\alpha x{e}^{2x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\alpha (x{e}^{2x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\alpha ({e}^{2x}+2x{e}^{2x}) \\\\  & =\\alpha (1+2x){e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\alpha (1+2x){e}^{2x})-2\\alpha x{e}^{2x} & =6{e}^{2x} \\\\ (1+2x-2x)\\alpha {e}^{2x} & =6{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\alpha {e}^{2x} & =6{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\alpha  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=6x{e}^{2x}.\n$$" 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186307604 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420161 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186307604 1078 #edb/ref 17592186305153 13194139534357 17592186045417 false] [17592186307604 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420161 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186307722 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420160 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186307722 1078 #edb/ref 17592186307030 13194139534357 17592186045417 false] [17592186307722 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420160 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186308275 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420162 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186308275 1078 #edb/ref 17592186306441 13194139534357 17592186045417 false] [17592186308275 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420162 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420167 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420168 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420169 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420170 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1043 #edb/ref 17592186420171 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1045 "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs With Exponential Forcing" 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1046 #edb/ref 17592186420169 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049146 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420159 1053 #uuid "bc665116-5a76-55aa-9353-754f3071777d" 13194139534357 17592186045417 true] [17592186420160